#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:82
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Channel moderators can end the conference, lock or unlock new admission, "
"mute microphones, turn participant cameras off, stop and temporarily block "
"screen sharing, use bulk mute/camera-off for lower-ranked participants, "
"allow raised-hand participants to speak, and remove users from both the "
"conference and the channel when channel policy allows it. Participants can "
"raise a hand when they need to speak; moderators see the request queue and "
"allowing speech unmutes the participant. A locked conference keeps users in "
"the channel but blocks non-moderators from joining the call. Camera or "
"screen sharing disabled by moderation is shown differently from a "
"participant turning it off voluntarily. Destructive and bulk actions ask for"
" confirmation first. Administrative events are recorded with the conference "
"and relevant events appear as system messages in the channel without turning"
" media/presence updates into chat spam."
msgstr ""
"Channel moderators can end the conference, lock or unlock new admission, "
"mute microphones, turn participant cameras off, stop and temporarily block "
"screen sharing, use bulk mute/camera-off for lower-ranked participants, "
"allow raised-hand participants to speak, and remove users from both the "
"conference and the channel when channel policy allows it. Participants can "
"raise a hand when they need to speak; moderators see the request queue and "
"allowing speech unmutes the participant. A locked conference keeps users in "
"the channel but blocks non-moderators from joining the call. Camera or "
"screen sharing disabled by moderation is shown differently from a "
"participant turning it off voluntarily. Destructive and bulk actions ask for"
" confirmation first. Administrative events are recorded with the conference "
"and relevant events appear as system messages in the channel without turning"
" media/presence updates into chat spam."

