#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_media_devices.html.heex:9
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The P2P setup dialog lists microphone, camera, and speaker choices before "
"sending or accepting an invite. During an active call, open Devices from the"
" Call toolbar to choose a different microphone, camera, or audio output."
msgstr ""
"The P2P setup dialog lists microphone, camera, and speaker choices before "
"sending or accepting an invite. During an active call, open Devices from the"
" Call toolbar to choose a different microphone, camera, or audio output."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:27
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The PM Is the Conversation"
msgstr "The PM Is the Conversation"

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:34
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The Status Bar Area"
msgstr "The Status Bar Area"

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:66
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The conference window shows explicit states while waiting for participants, "
"joining receive-only, recovering media, or handling a failed connection. "
"Recoverable failures keep the call open and expose Retry; leaving from a "
"warning or error still uses the confirmation dialog so microphone, camera "
"and SFU cleanup stay predictable."
msgstr ""
"The conference window shows explicit states while waiting for participants, "
"joining receive-only, recovering media, or handling a failed connection. "
"Recoverable failures keep the call open and expose Retry; leaving from a "
"warning or error still uses the confirmation dialog so microphone, camera "
"and SFU cleanup stay predictable."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_audio_call.html.heex:41
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The header and status bar show call duration, quality, active facets and "
"relay privacy. The peer list is intentionally compact because P2P is always "
"one-to-one."
msgstr ""
"The header and status bar show call duration, quality, active facets and "
"relay privacy. The peer list is intentionally compact because P2P is always "
"one-to-one."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_network_stats.html.heex:9
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The header shows the peer, session state, browser/WebRTC state, peer online "
"state, active call/file/game facets and whether the privacy relay is active."
msgstr ""
"The header shows the peer, session state, browser/WebRTC state, peer online "
"state, active call/file/game facets and whether the privacy relay is active."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:18
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The pre-join dialog lets you preview your camera, choose microphone, camera "
"and speaker devices, and decide whether to join with microphone or camera "
"enabled. Permission and device failures show a Retry action, and you can "
"still join receive-only. Layout and media defaults are remembered for your "
"account; browser-specific device choices are remembered locally."
msgstr ""
"The pre-join dialog lets you preview your camera, choose microphone, camera "
"and speaker devices, and decide whether to join with microphone or camera "
"enabled. Permission and device failures show a Retry action, and you can "
"still join receive-only. Layout and media defaults are remembered for your "
"account; browser-specific device choices are remembered locally."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:9
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Type /p2p <nick> (or use the nicklist context menu) to open setup before "
"sending an invite. Confirming setup sends the invite card in the private "
"message; the invited person clicks Accept to start their own setup and join "
"in place, or Decline to refuse — the inviter is told either way."
msgstr ""
"Type /p2p <nick> (or use the nicklist context menu) to open setup before "
"sending an invite. Confirming setup sends the invite card in the private "
"message; the invited person clicks Accept to start their own setup and join "
"in place, or Decline to refuse — the inviter is told either way."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_video_call.html.heex:16
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use the layout controls for Auto, Focus, Split, Speaker and Compact views. "
"Click the remote tile to focus it. The self-view button cycles your own "
"video between tile, picture-in-picture and hidden."
msgstr ""
"Use the layout controls for Auto, Focus, Split, Speaker and Compact views. "
"Click the remote tile to focus it. The self-view button cycles your own "
"video between tile, picture-in-picture and hidden."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:58
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use the reaction buttons in the conference toolbar to send a short visual "
"reaction. Reactions are ephemeral, appear on participant tiles and rows, are"
" not stored as chat messages, and are lightly rate limited to avoid spam."
msgstr ""
"Use the reaction buttons in the conference toolbar to send a short visual "
"reaction. Reactions are ephemeral, appear on participant tiles and rows, are"
" not stored as chat messages, and are lightly rate limited to avoid spam."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:42
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use the screen share button in the conference toolbar to publish your "
"selected screen or window. The shared screen replaces your outgoing camera "
"video while it is active, becomes the focused conference tile, and returns "
"to camera when you stop sharing or the browser ends capture."
msgstr ""
"Use the screen share button in the conference toolbar to publish your "
"selected screen or window. The shared screen replaces your outgoing camera "
"video while it is active, becomes the focused conference tile, and returns "
"to camera when you stop sharing or the browser ends capture."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:10
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"When a channel has an active conference, the Call control shows a live badge"
" with state, participant count and elapsed time. The info button opens a "
"summary with participants, current speaker when available, media icons and a"
" Join/Open action. Channel tabs and the conversations sidebar also show a "
"compact conference glyph."
msgstr ""
"When a channel has an active conference, the Call control shows a live badge"
" with state, participant count and elapsed time. The info button opens a "
"summary with participants, current speaker when available, media icons and a"
" Join/Open action. Channel tabs and the conversations sidebar also show a "
"compact conference glyph."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:34
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"When a conference is active, use Ctrl+Shift+ArrowUp to mute or unmute your "
"microphone, Ctrl+Shift+ArrowLeft to start or stop your camera, "
"Ctrl+Shift+ArrowRight to cycle layouts, Ctrl+Shift+ArrowDown to focus the "
"next participant, and Ctrl+Shift+Q to open the leave confirmation. Hold "
"Ctrl+Shift+Z for push-to-talk while muted. Conference shortcuts do not fire "
"from editable text fields."
msgstr ""
"When a conference is active, use Ctrl+Shift+ArrowUp to mute or unmute your "
"microphone, Ctrl+Shift+ArrowLeft to start or stop your camera, "
"Ctrl+Shift+ArrowRight to cycle layouts, Ctrl+Shift+ArrowDown to focus the "
"next participant, and Ctrl+Shift+Q to open the leave confirmation. Hold "
"Ctrl+Shift+Z for push-to-talk while muted. Conference shortcuts do not fire "
"from editable text fields."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:63
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"When the server has a TURN relay configured, the setup dialog or Toggle "
"Privacy Mode in the P2P menu can force the whole connection through the "
"relay, so your IP address is never shared with your peer. The preference is "
"remembered for future sessions."
msgstr ""
"When the server has a TURN relay configured, the setup dialog or Toggle "
"Privacy Mode in the P2P menu can force the whole connection through the "
"relay, so your IP address is never shared with your peer. The preference is "
"remembered for future sessions."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:56
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"You can hold one P2P session at a time. Accepting a new invite — or inviting"
" someone else — while a session is active asks whether to end the current "
"one first; any call, transfer or game in progress stops when you switch."
msgstr ""
"You can hold one P2P session at a time. Accepting a new invite — or inviting"
" someone else — while a session is active asks whether to end the current "
"one first; any call, transfer or game in progress stops when you switch."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_audio_call.html.heex:28
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"to stop your media call. The P2P session remains available for private "
"messages, files, games and statistics until you end the session itself."
msgstr ""
"to stop your media call. The P2P session remains available for private "
"messages, files, games and statistics until you end the session itself."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_network_stats.html.heex:53
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "— resolution and frame rate of the received video or screen stream."
msgstr "— resolution and frame rate of the received video or screen stream."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_call_quality.html.heex:12
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Calls use conservative audio and video limits by default to favor stability "
"over maximum image quality."
msgstr ""
"Calls use conservative audio and video limits by default to favor stability "
"over maximum image quality."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:29
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Messages during the session are regular private messages, saved like any "
"other. Session events — connected, file received, game score, who ended it —"
" are written into the PM history as P2P lines, so the story of the session "
"survives it. While a session exists, the peer's PM tab, PM sidebar row and "
"PM topic bar show the same P2P indicator family used by channel conferences,"
" with state and active call/file/game/relay facets."
msgstr ""
"Messages during the session are regular private messages, saved like any "
"other. Session events — connected, file received, game score, who ended it —"
" are written into the PM history as P2P lines, so the story of the session "
"survives it. While a session exists, the peer's PM tab, PM sidebar row and "
"PM topic bar show the same P2P indicator family used by channel conferences,"
" with state and active call/file/game/relay facets."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_call_quality.html.heex:1
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Monitor connection quality during calls."
msgstr "Monitor connection quality during calls."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_call_quality.html.heex:10
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Stable Defaults"
msgstr "Stable Defaults"

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_audio_call.html.heex:6
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
". Either peer can start or stop their own microphone independently; if your "
"peer starts media first, your Call section opens and you join automatically."
msgstr ""
". Either peer can start or stop their own microphone independently; if your "
"peer starts media first, your Call section opens and you join automatically."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_universal_lobby.html.heex:23
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Closing the P2P Session Console disconnects the whole session (after a "
"confirmation); minimizing keeps everything running in the taskbar. The "
"status bar always shows the active session — click it to bring the console "
"back to the front."
msgstr ""
"Closing the P2P Session Console disconnects the whole session (after a "
"confirmation); minimizing keeps everything running in the taskbar. The "
"status bar always shows the active session — click it to bring the console "
"back to the front."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_video_call.html.heex:35
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Ctrl+Shift+. toggles screen sharing when the P2P Session Console is focused."
" A shared screen automatically favors the focus layout."
msgstr ""
"Ctrl+Shift+. toggles screen sharing when the P2P Session Console is focused."
" A shared screen automatically favors the focus layout."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_audio_call.html.heex:34
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Ctrl+Shift+Q in the focused P2P Session Console ends only the call media. "
"Use the status bar stop button or close confirmation to end the whole P2P "
"session."
msgstr ""
"Ctrl+Shift+Q in the focused P2P Session Console ends only the call media. "
"Use the status bar stop button or close confirmation to end the whole P2P "
"session."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:22
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Once connected, the P2P menu in the menu bar (mirrored in the Start menu) "
"opens the P2P Session Console. Its sections cover Call for audio/video, "
"Files for transfers, Games for the two-player arcade, and Stats for live "
"telemetry. The console opens on activity: an incoming file offer selects "
"Files, a game proposal selects Games, and when your peer turns their camera "
"or microphone on the Call section surfaces and you join automatically."
msgstr ""
"Once connected, the P2P menu in the menu bar (mirrored in the Start menu) "
"opens the P2P Session Console. Its sections cover Call for audio/video, "
"Files for transfers, Games for the two-player arcade, and Stats for live "
"telemetry. The console opens on activity: an incoming file offer selects "
"Files, a game proposal selects Games, and when your peer turns their camera "
"or microphone on the Call section surfaces and you join automatically."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_universal_lobby.html.heex:9
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Once connected, the call starts automatically with each side's setup choices"
" and the console keeps Files, Games and Stats one tap away. Everything runs "
"concurrently over the same connection: share your screen, send a file during"
" the call, start a game without hanging up. Ending any one activity never "
"drops the others — only ending the session does."
msgstr ""
"Once connected, the call starts automatically with each side's setup choices"
" and the console keeps Files, Games and Stats one tap away. Everything runs "
"concurrently over the same connection: share your screen, send a file during"
" the call, start a game without hanging up. Ending any one activity never "
"drops the others — only ending the session does."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:2
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"P2P sessions run right inside the chat: the invite, the conversation and the"
" P2P Session Console live on the chat desktop, anchored to the private "
"message with your peer."
msgstr ""
"P2P sessions run right inside the chat: the invite, the conversation and the"
" P2P Session Console live on the chat desktop, anchored to the private "
"message with your peer."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:43
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The Call section uses the same media language as channel conferences: mic, "
"camera, screen share, devices, PiP, layout, self-view, mini mode, statistics"
" and reaction controls are icon buttons with tooltips. End Call stops only "
"the media; closing the P2P Session Console asks before ending the whole P2P "
"session."
msgstr ""
"The Call section uses the same media language as channel conferences: mic, "
"camera, screen share, devices, PiP, layout, self-view, mini mode, statistics"
" and reaction controls are icon buttons with tooltips. End Call stops only "
"the media; closing the P2P Session Console asks before ending the whole P2P "
"session."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_universal_lobby.html.heex:2
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The P2P Lobby is the persistent peer-to-peer connection behind /p2p: one "
"link between two users that hosts a call, file transfers and games all at "
"the same time. It lives inside the chat — setup happens before sending or "
"accepting the invite, and accepting opens the P2P Session Console right on "
"the chat desktop, next to your conversations."
msgstr ""
"The P2P Lobby is the persistent peer-to-peer connection behind /p2p: one "
"link between two users that hosts a call, file transfers and games all at "
"the same time. It lives inside the chat — setup happens before sending or "
"accepting the invite, and accepting opens the P2P Session Console right on "
"the chat desktop, next to your conversations."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:20
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The Session Console"
msgstr "The Session Console"

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_network_stats.html.heex:2
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The Stats section of the P2P Session Console shows live telemetry for the "
"whole P2P session: WebRTC connection, audio, video or screen source, file "
"transfer and game data channels. Click the ? button in the panel to see a "
"short explanation of each metric inline, or hover any row for a tooltip."
msgstr ""
"The Stats section of the P2P Session Console shows live telemetry for the "
"whole P2P session: WebRTC connection, audio, video or screen source, file "
"transfer and game data channels. Click the ? button in the panel to see a "
"short explanation of each metric inline, or hover any row for a tooltip."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:90
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The conference Stats section lives inside the same call window and shows "
"both server-side SFU state and live browser connection metrics. Use the "
"Stats tab in the conference header to inspect diagnostics without leaving "
"the call surface. Closing the conference window leaves the conference, so "
"minimize it to keep the session running."
msgstr ""
"The conference Stats section lives inside the same call window and shows "
"both server-side SFU state and live browser connection metrics. Use the "
"Stats tab in the conference header to inspect diagnostics without leaving "
"the call surface. Closing the conference window leaves the conference, so "
"minimize it to keep the session running."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:36
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The status bar always shows your active session, wherever you are in the "
"chat. It also shows compact badges for active call, file transfer, game, "
"call quality and relay privacy. Click it to bring the P2P Session Console to"
" the front; the stop button next to it cancels a pending invite or ends the "
"session, after a confirmation."
msgstr ""
"The status bar always shows your active session, wherever you are in the "
"chat. It also shows compact badges for active call, file transfer, game, "
"call quality and relay privacy. Click it to bring the P2P Session Console to"
" the front; the stop button next to it cancels a pending invite or ends the "
"session, after a confirmation."

